From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lenOS hardening <hardening@lenos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] frameworks/base: add android.Manifest.permission.NETWORK to API surface

Adds the NETWORK permission constant to core/api/current.txt (android.Manifest
$permission class). REQUIRED for fwb-0001 (permission declaration) to compile:
PermissionMonitor.java in the Connectivity module does
`import static android.Manifest.permission.NETWORK`, and the build's API check
fails if a new public constant appears without a current.txt entry.

Alphabetically placed between NEARBY_WIFI_DEVICES and NFC, matching how the
other Manifest.permission constants are ordered.

Without this entry, the build fails with an "API changed; run update-api"
error. With it, android.Manifest.permission.NETWORK is a public SDK constant.
---
diff --git a/core/api/current.txt b/core/api/current.txt
--- a/core/api/current.txt
+++ b/core/api/current.txt
@@ -241,6 +241,7 @@
     field public static final String MOUNT_FORMAT_FILESYSTEMS = "android.permission.MOUNT_FORMAT_FILESYSTEMS";
     field public static final String MOUNT_UNMOUNT_FILESYSTEMS = "android.permission.MOUNT_UNMOUNT_FILESYSTEMS";
     field public static final String NEARBY_WIFI_DEVICES = "android.permission.NEARBY_WIFI_DEVICES";
+    field public static final String NETWORK = "android.permission.NETWORK";
     field public static final String NFC = "android.permission.NFC";
     field public static final String NFC_PREFERRED_PAYMENT_INFO = "android.permission.NFC_PREFERRED_PAYMENT_INFO";
     field public static final String NFC_TRANSACTION_EVENT = "android.permission.NFC_TRANSACTION_EVENT";
diff --git a/core/api/lint-baseline.txt b/core/api/lint-baseline.txt
--- a/core/api/lint-baseline.txt
+++ b/core/api/lint-baseline.txt
@@ -1726,3 +1726,5 @@
     New API must be flagged with @FlaggedApi: method android.view.inputmethod.InlineSuggestionsRequest.Builder.setClientSupported(boolean)
 UnflaggedApi: android.view.inputmethod.InlineSuggestionsRequest.Builder#setServiceSupported(boolean):
     New API must be flagged with @FlaggedApi: method android.view.inputmethod.InlineSuggestionsRequest.Builder.setServiceSupported(boolean)
+UnflaggedApi: android.Manifest.permission#NETWORK:
+    New API must be flagged with @FlaggedApi: field android.Manifest.permission.NETWORK
